# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo and on checkout (all platforms).
# Biome formats to LF; without this, Windows checkouts get CRLF and lint fails.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalize.
*.node binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
bun.lock -text

# Whole-file regenerations of the module graph (scripts/gen-tree-map.mjs / `just map`). Any two
# PRs that add or move a module conflict here by construction — the leading "scale" line and the
# full edge list are recomputed from EVERY tracked module, not just the ones a given PR touched.
# `merge=regenerate` only NAMES the driver; its definition lives in this clone's local git config,
# set by scripts/setup-git-merge-driver.mjs (runs automatically via `bun install`'s `prepare`
# script) — see scripts/check-merge-driver.mjs for why a .gitattributes-only change here would be
# silently vacuous. The driver (scripts/merge-drivers/defer-regeneration.mjs) does NOT re-run the
# generator itself — see that file's header for why that's unsafe mid-merge — it just avoids
# leaving conflict markers in machine-generated content; `just map-check` (CI's ci-docgen) is what
# actually catches the resulting staleness and forces a `just map` + commit. docgen's own generated
# marker regions (README.md, docs/wiki/*.md, etc.) are deliberately NOT listed here: they carry the
# same shape of aggregate summary line, but are keyed to a much narrower, much less frequently
# touched namespace (tools/config keys/metrics) and have not been a measured source of conflicts
# the way this pair has.
TREE.md merge=regenerate
docs/dependency-graph.json merge=regenerate
